  <prompt>ArmDeploymentRunner.cs's file-header "BLOCKING DISCOVERY" note (task 123, 2026-08-19) documents that infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep -- the ONLY Bicep template exercised in production today (Model2Dedicated branch) -- deploys Key Vault + Storage + Service Bus + Cosmos + membership-topic + optional ACS + optional SignalR, but declares NO User-Assigned Managed Identity and NO App Service resource. `userAssignedIdentityResourceId` is a dead pass-through parameter (task 027) that no resource binds to. BicepDeployOutputs.cs's REQUIRED string properties UserAssignedIdentityObjectId/UserAssignedIdentityClientId/AppServiceName/AppServiceStagingSlotName therefore always map to empty string on a real deploy, which H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler.AreOutputsComplete() correctly (honestly) reports as BicepDeployOutputsIncomplete. Grep-verified: modules/uami.bicep (task 028) and modules/app-service.bicep + modules/app-service-slot.bicep + modules/app-service-plan.bicep (task 029) already exist, are purpose-built for exactly this per-customer stamp (their own header comments name customer.bicep as the intended caller), and are currently ORPHANED -- zero live consumers (only platform-controlplane.bicep uses uami.bicep + app-service-plan.bicep, for the L2 control-plane's OWN App Service, a different deployment; only the stale, CI-uncompiled stacks/model2-full.bicep uses app-service.bicep). Wire these four EXISTING modules into customer.bicep. Do NOT author new files (`modules/customer-uami.bicep` / `modules/customer-appservice.bicep`) -- that would violate CLAUDE.md §11's reuse mandate against code that already exists, is correct, and is purpose-built for this exact call site.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Bicep module composition, ADR-028 UAMI-only identity binding, and design.md §7 resource-naming/deployment-order conformance.</role>

  <goal>customer.bicep creates ONE per-customer UAMI (via the existing modules/uami.bicep) and binds it -- via modules/app-service-plan.bicep + modules/app-service.bicep + modules/app-service-slot.bicep, all pre-existing and unmodified -- to a BFF App Service with BOTH a production slot and a staging slot, matching design.md §7.1's canonical naming and §7.6's deployment order. customer.bicep's outputs expose userAssignedIdentityResourceId/userAssignedIdentityObjectId/userAssignedIdentityClientId/appServiceName/appServiceStagingSlotName under EXACTLY those names so ArmDeploymentRunner.MapOutputs (task 123, unmodified by this task) stops mapping them to empty string on a real ARM deploy.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 123 (H2a ARM.Resources deployment SDK port, completed 2026-08-19) surfaced this gap while porting the real ArmDeployment.CreateOrUpdateAsync call -- it did NOT attempt to fix customer.bicep itself (declared out of that task's SDK-port scope) but left a detailed, evidence-cited header comment in ArmDeploymentRunner.cs documenting exactly which BicepDeployOutputs fields cannot be populated and why. The project owner reviewed this + task 126's parallel discovery (see task 129) and chose Path 1: author dedicated Bicep-completion tasks (127/128/129) BEFORE dispatching Wave G-3's H3/H8/H9 handler ports, since H3 (task 130) needs a real per-customer App Service to exist before its Entra app-reg / consent work is meaningfully testable end-to-end.</background>
