  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 (Component Justification -- Default to Reuse)">modules/uami.bicep, modules/app-service.bicep, modules/app-service-slot.bicep, modules/app-service-plan.bicep already exist, are correct (task 028/029, unmodified since), and are purpose-built for exactly this per-customer stamp (grep their header comments -- they name customer.bicep as the intended caller). MUST invoke these EXISTING modules unmodified. MUST NOT author new `modules/customer-uami.bicep` / `modules/customer-appservice.bicep` files -- that duplicates working code and fails the Existing-question test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design.md §7.1 (authoritative naming table, v3.2)">UAMI name MUST be `mi-spaarke-{customerId}-{environmentName}` -- NOT the `sprk-{env}-{customerId}-uami` pattern suggested in uami.bicep's own inline header comment (that comment predates design.md's v3.2 naming-table finalization and is stale aspirational text, not the canonical source). App Service Plan name MUST be `sprk-{customerId}-{environmentName}-plan`; App Service name MUST be `sprk-{customerId}-{environmentName}-api`. Per root CLAUDE.md §2, code wins over stale doc-comments, but design.md's naming table is the CURRENT, actively-maintained design source (loaded every task per this project's CLAUDE.md) and takes precedence over a task-028-era inline comment that nothing has kept in sync.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design.md §7.6 (Deployment Order)">UAMI (step 2) MUST be declared before Key Vault (step 4) in the resource-declaration sequence for readability/order-of-intent, even though Bicep's dependency graph does not strictly require textual ordering. App Service Plan (step 9) + App Service (step 14) belong near the end of the resource section, after the AI/data services.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 MUST rules / app-service.bicep's own header note">MUST NOT co-emit SystemAssigned alongside UserAssigned (`type: 'SystemAssigned, UserAssigned'`) -- app-service.bicep already enforces UAMI-only by construction; do not add a SystemAssigned block anywhere in this task's changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md MUST rules / task 125 (H4, already shipped)">The `keyVaultReferenceIdentity` PATCH on both slots (T1) is H4's post-deploy job (ArmAppServiceIdentityPatcher, task 125, already shipped) -- Bicep's job here is ONLY to bind the UAMI to both slots' `identity.userAssignedIdentities` block (which app-service.bicep/app-service-slot.bicep already do by construction once a UAMI resource id is passed in). Do NOT attempt a keyVaultReferenceIdentity PATCH in Bicep.</constraint>
    <constraint source="key-vault.bicep line 55-56 (existing unused param)">key-vault.bicep ALREADY has a `userAssignedIdentityPrincipalId` param that grants Key Vault Secrets User when non-empty. This task MUST pass `uami.outputs.principalId` into the EXISTING `keyVault` module invocation in customer.bicep (a one-line addition to an existing module call) rather than hand-rolling a new role-assignment resource or reusing `modules/role-assignment-keyvault.bicep` redundantly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 027 cleanup (this task supersedes it)">The existing `userAssignedIdentityResourceId` INPUT parameter (customer.bicep, default empty, "no resource in THIS module binds to it yet") and its dead output echo become vestigial once this task lands a REAL UAMI creation. Remove the input parameter and its docstring; replace the output with the real `uami.outputs.id` value under the SAME output name (`userAssignedIdentityResourceId`) so downstream consumers see no name-level breaking change, only a real value where there was previously always empty.</constraint>
    <constraint source="parallel-safety with task 128 (both amend customer.bicep concurrently)">This task OWNS: (a) the top-of-file insertion between the Resource Group block and the Key Vault module block (new UAMI module + the key-vault module's added param), and (b) a NEW section inserted after the existing SignalR section and before OUTPUTS (App Service Plan + App Service + App Service Slot modules + their new params). This task MUST NOT touch the Cosmos DB / Membership Topic / ACS section of the file -- that is task 128's insertion zone (a new AI-services section between Cosmos DB and Membership Topic). If task 128 has already landed when this task executes, rebase around its section rather than reordering it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

