  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read customer.bicep in full (350 lines), uami.bicep, app-service.bicep, app-service-slot.bicep, app-service-plan.bicep, key-vault.bicep (params only), and design.md §7.1/§7.2/§7.6.</step>
    <step order="1" name="UAMI">Add `module uami 'modules/uami.bicep'` invoked with `scope: rg`, name `mi-spaarke-${customerId}-${environmentName}` per design.md §7.1, `location`, `tags`. Insert between the Resource Group block and the Key Vault module block.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Key Vault RBAC wiring">Add `userAssignedIdentityPrincipalId: uami.outputs.principalId` to the EXISTING `keyVault` module invocation's params block (one-line addition; do not touch any other keyVault param).</step>
    <step order="3" name="App Service Plan + App Service + Slot">Add a new section (after the existing SignalR section, before OUTPUTS) invoking modules/app-service-plan.bicep (`sprk-${customerId}-${environmentName}-plan`, new `appServiceSku` param default `'S1'` matching design.md §7.2's default SKU), modules/app-service.bicep (`sprk-${customerId}-${environmentName}-api`, `userAssignedIdentityResourceId: uami.outputs.id`, minimal/empty `appSettings` -- do NOT invent Dataverse/Communication/AI app-settings that require params customer.bicep does not declare; H5/H6/H7 own writing those at runtime per the discovery note this task closes), and modules/app-service-slot.bicep (`slotName: 'staging'`, the SAME `uami.outputs.id`).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Remove vestigial pass-through param">Delete the `userAssignedIdentityResourceId` INPUT parameter (task 027, default empty, dead) and its docstring. Replace the existing `output userAssignedIdentityResourceId string = userAssignedIdentityResourceId` echo with `output userAssignedIdentityResourceId string = uami.outputs.id`.</step>
    <step order="5" name="New outputs">Add, under EXACTLY these names (matching BicepDeployOutputs.cs / ArmDeploymentRunner.MapOutputs): `output userAssignedIdentityObjectId string = uami.outputs.principalId`, `output userAssignedIdentityClientId string = uami.outputs.clientId`, `output appServiceName string = bffApi.outputs.appServiceName`, `output appServiceStagingSlotName string = bffApiSlot.outputs.slotName` (name your module symbols `bffApi` / `bffApiSlot` or update these references to match your actual symbol names).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Validate">`az bicep build --file infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep --outfile infrastructure/bicep/customer.json` -- 0 errors, 0 warnings. Commit the regenerated customer.json alongside customer.bicep.</step>
    <step order="7" name="What-if (or documented deferral)">If live Azure reachability is available in this execution context, run `az deployment sub what-if` against a representative parameter set and confirm the 4 new resources (UAMI, plan, App Service, slot) show as Create with no unexpected changes to the 6 existing resources. If not reachable (sandbox), document this as a deferred live-ceremony step in the task's completion notes, per the precedent set by tasks 108/123/125.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>spec.md FR-04 ("Six new module invocations vs current Provision-Customer.ps1 step 3: Cosmos DB + OpenAI + AI Search + Document Intelligence + App Insights/Log Analytics + optional SignalR") and design.md §7.2 rows 11-12 additionally require Document Intelligence + App Insights/Log Analytics modules wired into customer.bicep. This is a REAL gap the owner's Gap-1 description (UAMI + App Service only) does not cover, and it is OUTSIDE this task's declared scope. Do NOT silently expand this task to add those two resources. STOP and flag to the project owner in this task's completion notes whether a follow-on task should be authored (a natural "task 127b" or folded into a future wave) -- see task 129's notes for the downstream consequence (2 of kv-secrets.generated.bicep's ~15 FromBicepOutput entries cannot resolve without these resources).</trigger>
    <trigger>If design.md §7.1's UAMI naming pattern (`mi-spaarke-{customerId}-{env}`) would collide with, or orphan, a LIVE UAMI or System-Assigned-MI-based App Service already deployed for an existing customer under the pre-Phase-C interim scheme (design.md §7.2 row 2's "interim state" caveat), STOP and escalate before applying -- do not silently rename or duplicate a live identity.</trigger>
  </escalation>

