  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- modules/uami.bicep + modules/app-service.bicep + modules/app-service-slot.bicep + modules/app-service-plan.bicep already exist, are correct, and are purpose-built for this exact call site (their own header comments name customer.bicep as the intended caller); key-vault.bicep already has an unused RBAC-wiring param waiting for exactly this UAMI. Extension -- wiring four already-built, already-tested modules into an existing composition is the minimal, correct move; authoring new files would duplicate working code. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H2a's ArmDeploymentRunner cannot populate 4 of its 9 required BicepDeployOutputs fields on any real customer deploy (honest empty-string per the file-header discovery note), and H3/H8/H9/H10 (Wave G-3/G-4, all downstream of a real App Service + UAMI existing) cannot be meaningfully live-verified until this lands -- this is why the owner chose Path 1 (fix Bicep before dispatching Wave G-3).</notes>

  <execution>
